cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Plug and Prey: a factory-backdoored Android TV box and its BadBox C2"
message: "If you use this research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Moraga
    given-names: Patricio
  - family-names: De La Paz
    given-names: Anthony
abstract: >-
  Threat intelligence case study of a mass-market Allwinner Android TV box that
  ships already rooted and already implanted. A BadBox-class command-and-control
  client lives inside system_server, loaded from a framework image whose source
  jar has been deleted; its operator address is Base64-, XOR-, and AES-encrypted
  and assembled only in memory at call time. The public edition publishes
  network indicators in defanged form and withholds cryptographic keys,
  decrypted payloads, and device identifiers because the implant persists in
  the field. Presented at ekoparty 2026.
keywords:
  - threat-intelligence
  - badbox
  - supply-chain
  - android-tv
  - command-and-control
  - residential-proxy
